github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6220#issuecomment-5534560415","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSeL2AQ","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Redirect restores source context <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>During <b><i>follow_redirects=True</i></b>, Werkzeug recursively calls <b><i>FlaskClient.open</i></b>, so the pending list\n>contains the source context followed by the destination context. Replaying with <b><i>pop()</i></b> enters the\n>destination first and source last, leaving <b><i>request</i></b> bound to the redirect source instead of the\n>final response.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/testing.py[244]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6220/files#diff-8b6ebc456dd7ce1ab0df544ee20d38211b947ad84e600b2727e4dd5db9fe913eR244-R244)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+            self._context_stack.enter_context(self._new_contexts.pop())\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>Flask installs <b><i>_new_contexts.append</i></b> as the preservation callback, and <b><i>wsgi_app</i></b> invokes it for\n>every request before popping that request&#x27;s context. Werkzeug&#x27;s redirect implementation calls\n><b><i>self.open(...)</i></b>, dynamically re-entering <b><i>FlaskClient.open</i></b> before the outer call reaches its\n>replay block; consequently, a one-hop redirect accumulates <b><i>[source, destination]</i></b>. The changed\n><b><i>pop()</i></b> loop enters destination and then source, while <b><i>AppContext.push</i></b> makes each newly entered\n>context active, so the source is exposed after the final response; the prior FIFO loop left\n>destination active.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/testing.py[185-189]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/ce371565d0889138abb2c2c60e02e59714dbf2c9/src/flask/testing.py/#L185-L189)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[1595-1619]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/ce371565d0889138abb2c2c60e02e59714dbf2c9/src/flask/app.py/#L1595-L1619)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/ctx.py[416-434]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/ce371565d0889138abb2c2c60e02e59714dbf2c9/src/flask/ctx.py/#L416-L434)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/testing.py[230-245]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/ce371565d0889138abb2c2c60e02e59714dbf2c9/src/flask/testing.py/#L230-L245)</code>\n> <code>🌐 [Werkzeug&#x27;s current `Client.resolve_redirect` implementation follows the redirect by returning `self.open(builder, buffered=buffered)`.](https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/blob/main/src/werkzeug/test.py)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Preserved contexts are appended in request order, but replaying them with `list.pop()` reverses that order. For a followed redirect, the source context becomes active instead of the final destination context.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>Werkzeug follows redirects by recursively dispatching through `self.open`. Preserve FIFO entry order, and add a regression test asserting that `request.path` refers to the final redirect destination inside a preserving client block.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/testing.py[230-245]\n>- tests/test_testing.py[367-381]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n<!-- qodo-context:start -->\n<details><summary><strong>Context sources</strong></summary>\n\n<div>&#x2705; Web pages:</div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/blob/005812d545065b36be11b60229cedfb125d80cbd/src/werkzeug/test.py\"><code>🌐 src/werkzeug/test.py at 005812d545065b36be11b60229cedfb125d80cbd · pallets/werkzeug</code></a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/pallets/werkzeug/blob/0644c6263b1b3b6705426782c1b39a15e04450af/werkzeug/test.py\"><code>🌐 werkzeug/test.py</code></a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://werkzeug.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/test/\"><code>🌐 https://werkzeug.palletsprojects.com/en/stable/test/</code></a></div>\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<code>+6 more</code></div>\n<div>Review mode: <code>⚖️ Balanced</code>: This is a small but behavioral change in Flask testing context management, where ordering and compatibility edge cases warrant a complete single-pass review.</div>\n<!-- qodo-context:end -->\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n\n\n<!-- qodo-daily-tip:start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Tip of the day</strong></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n<pre>💡 Did you know, you can route each action level your way: inline, summary, both, or drop</pre>\n\n<a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai/tips-and-tricks\">More tips ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://app.qodo.ai/configurations?tab=display-preferences\">Customize Qodo ↗</a> | <a href=\"https://docs.qodo.ai\">Qodo docs ↗</a>\n\n</details>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n<!